# Code Simplification

{%- include "templates/.harness/skills-shared/objective-control/CONTROL." ~ harness_language ~ ".md.jinja" %}

Preserve behavior and the start-to-goal flow while reducing unnecessary code. Large line count is a diagnostic, not a verdict. Do not refactor unrelated code and do not trade clarity for clever compression.

The final necessity report covers every added code line by semantic portion: path/range, why it exists, objective, inputs, outputs, real evidence, simpler alternative considered, and why the retained portion is necessary. Remove or simplify portions without proven behavior. Vague whole-file justification is invalid: each receipt must include added code, span at most 120 physical lines, and use a non-no-op evidence command. This limit controls evidence granularity, not implementation size. If simplification changes files, return through planning, incremental execution, validation and a fresh local commit before quality and adversarial review; an older commit cannot prove the simplification.
